WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.520
Welcome to The Test Set. Here we talk with some of the brightest thinkers and tinkerers

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:11.440
in statistical analysis, scientific computing, and machine learning. Digging into what makes

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:17.680
them tick, plus the insights, experiments, and OMG moments that shape the field.

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:22.400
In this episode, we talk with Leilani Battle, who likes things she can repeat, study, and

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:26.799
refine. Whether that means honing her disc golf skills, tweaking a recipe, or deriving

00:00:26.799 --> 00:00:32.439
the perfect vegan buttermilk sourdough pancakes. This same experimental instinct runs through

00:00:32.439 --> 00:00:36.880
her research at the University of Washington. Leilani built her career straddling two very

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:42.279
different research cultures, the computation behind databases and the human-centered, experimental

00:00:42.279 --> 00:00:47.160
world of visualization, an experience she describes as essentially getting a PhD in

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:51.959
two disciplines. We talk about the magic that happens when those fields meet, how what loads

00:00:51.959 --> 00:00:56.959
first in a visualization can shape what people find in their data, and how our work now applies

00:00:56.959 --> 00:01:02.000
that same technical and human perspective to responsible data science. So I'm so excited

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:03.560
for you to listen to Leilani.

